AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "CHEBI:50847") rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000296> "A classical agent (Freund's adjuvant, BCG, Corynebacterium parvum, et al.) contains bacterial antigens. It could also be endogenous (e.g., histamine, interferon, transfer factor, tuftsin, interleukin-1). Its mode of action is either non-specific, resulting in increased immune responsiveness to a wide variety of antigens, or antigen-specific, i.e., affecting a restricted type of immune response to a narrow group of antigens. The therapeutic efficacy is related to its antigen-specific immunoadjuvanticity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000296> "immune stimulant agent therapy")
